verses.text:
Your confederates have pushed you to the frontier;
your friends have tricked you and prevailed against you;
your table companions lay a snare{c} under you—
he has no discernment.

On that day, declares Yahweh,
will I not destroy the wise men out of Edom,
and understanding out of the mount of Esau?{d}

Your warriors will be dismayed, Teman,{e}
so that every man will be cut off from the mount of Esau
by slaughter.

You should not have entered my people’s gate
in the day of their calamity;
you, of all people, should not have gazed on his misery
in the day of his calamity;
you should not have reached for his goods
in the day of his calamity.{g}

For as you have drunk on my holy mountain,{i}
so all the nations will drink continually;
they will drink and swallow,
and will be as though they had never been.

But on Mount Zion there will be those who escape,
and it will be holy,
and the house of Jacob will possess its own possessions.{j}

The exiles of this army of Israel’s children
shall own Canaanite land up to Zarephath,{m}
and Jerusalem’s exiles in Sepharad{n}
shall have the towns of the Negev.
